CHAPTER III

< rr

RIGHTS OF VICTIMS Article 4

Every woman and child victim of violence has the right: a. to be respected for their dignity as a human being; b. to receive protection from family, community, Regional Government and/or other parties either temporarily or based on a protection order from the court;

c. to physical, psychological or sexual health recovery in accordance with the suffering experienced by victims of violence;

t. r l H .

d. to special handling related to victim confidentiality;

e. to accompaniment by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;

f. to spiritual guidance services; and

g. to make their own decisions.

Article 6

(1) The community has the obligation and responsibility to provide protection to women and children victims of violence.

(2) The obligations and responsibilities of the community as referred to in paragraph (1) are carried out in the form of:

a. preventing the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children;
b. providing protection to victims;
c. providing emergency assistance;
d. providing information and/or reporting acts of violence against women and children to the competent authorities; and
e. participating in handling victims of violence.

3.1.text:
Article 10

SPM as referred to in Article 9 has performance indicators including:

a. coverage of women and children victims of violence who receive complaint handling by trained officers in the integrated service unit;
b. coverage of women and children victims of violence who receive health services by trained health workers at Puskesmas and Hospitals;
c. coverage of Social Rehabilitation services provided by trained Social Rehabilitation officers for women and children victims of violence in the integrated service unit;
d. coverage of spiritual guidance services provided by trained spiritual guidance officers for women and children victims of violence in the integrated service unit;
e. coverage of law enforcement from the investigation level to court decisions on cases of violence against women and children;
f. coverage of women and children victims of violence who receive legal aid services;
g. coverage of repatriation services for women and children victims of violence; and
h. coverage of social reintegration services for women and children victims of violence.

CHAPTER V

INSTITUTIONS

:Article 7

(1) In providing protection for women and children victims of violence in the Region, the Regent may establish PPT.

(2) The establishment and development of PPT shall be adjusted to the development of priority needs, and the financial capacity of the Region as well as the institutional and personnel capacity existing in the Region.

(3) PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) may accommodate institutions/work units that provide services for victims of violence such as P2TP2A, Safe Houses, Children's Social Protection Houses, Trauma Center Protection Houses, Women's Social Protection Houses, Shelters and other service activities in accordance with the prevailing laws and regulations.

(4) Forms of services implemented by PPT, include:

a. complaints;
b. health rehabilitation;
c. social rehabilitation;
d. legal aid;
e. repatriation; and
f. social reintegration.
(5) In providing protection for women and children victims of violence, PPT is obligated to:
a. provide services as soon as possible and free of charge to Victims;
b. organize Protection and fulfillment of victims' rights to Health Rehabilitation, Social Rehabilitation, Repatriation, social reintegration and legal aid;
c. cooperate with certain institutions in providing translators and accompanying volunteers needed for Victims; establish networks with government or private hospitals for the treatment and health recovery of Victims and cooperate with Witness and Victim Protection agencies, social Protection houses or trauma centers owned by the government, community, or other institutions for the health recovery of victims;

r

e. provide ease, comfort, and safety for victims;

f. maintain the confidentiality of victims;

g. provide fulfillment of legal aid for victims; h. in the case of integrated service delivery being carried out in a network, PPT remains responsible for the entire referral process of services required by victims.

(6) The provision of integrated services as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be implemented in accordance with SPM.

