CHAPTER V

INSTITUTIONS

:Article 7

(1) In providing protection for women and children victims of violence in the Region, the Regent may establish PPT.

(2) The establishment and development of PPT shall be adjusted to the development of priority needs, and the financial capacity of the Region as well as the institutional and personnel capacity existing in the Region.

(3) PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) may accommodate institutions/work units that provide services for victims of violence such as P2TP2A, Safe Houses, Children's Social Protection Houses, Trauma Center Protection Houses, Women's Social Protection Houses, Shelters and other service activities in accordance with the prevailing laws and regulations.

(4) Forms of services implemented by PPT, include:

a. complaints;
b. health rehabilitation;
c. social rehabilitation;
d. legal aid;
e. repatriation; and
f. social reintegration.
(5) In providing protection for women and children victims of violence, PPT is obligated to:
a. provide services as soon as possible and free of charge to Victims;
b. organize Protection and fulfillment of victims' rights to Health Rehabilitation, Social Rehabilitation, Repatriation, social reintegration and legal aid;
c. cooperate with certain institutions in providing translators and accompanying volunteers needed for Victims; establish networks with government or private hospitals for the treatment and health recovery of Victims and cooperate with Witness and Victim Protection agencies, social Protection houses or trauma centers owned by the government, community, or other institutions for the health recovery of victims;

r

e. provide ease, comfort, and safety for victims;

f. maintain the confidentiality of victims;

g. provide fulfillment of legal aid for victims; h. in the case of integrated service delivery being carried out in a network, PPT remains responsible for the entire referral process of services required by victims.

(6) The provision of integrated services as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be implemented in accordance with SPM.

